  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Integrated Pest Management (IPM) in Abkhazia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Georgia):  .Georgia&apos;s self-reliance as a critical ally in the Caucasus region is threatened by the Russian occupation of Abkhazia.  This program will support the U.S. policy objective of restoring Georgia&apos;s territorial integrity by reducing the reliance of Abkhaz farmers on Russia and building their capacity to protect their livelihoods against the brown marmorated stink bug (BMSB) and other pests.  Abkhaz farmers&apos; livelihoods have been severely damaged in the past two years by the invasive and rapidly spreading stink bug, which has inflicted damage to crops essential to food security and income including hazelnuts, citrus, and corn...This program provides technical assistance and training to strengthen farmers&apos; ability throughout six districts of Abkhazia to apply integrated pest management (IPM) techniques to protect their crops against agricultural pests and access tools and resources to practice IPM effectively.  To institutionalize IPM systems, the program will also provide technical assistance to private sector stakeholders in Abkhazia, including input suppliers...A total of $170,000 in technical assistance will contribute to CAATSA Goal 8; by supporting Abkhaz farmers in this time of crisis and building their capacity to respond to future emergencies, the program will decrease Abkhaz dependence on Russian markets while also projecting American leadership through humanitarian relief (JSP 3.4) and strengthening relations between Georgia and its breakaway region (JRS 3.3).  These improved relations will help Georgia restore its territorial integrity, make Georgia a stronger and more stable ally for the United States (ICS Mission Goal 2), and increase U.S. influence in the region...This activity is implemented through a PIO grant with the UN since UN agencies are the only international entities able to operate in Abkhazia with diplomatic status.  The use of this PIO as an implementer has been approved by USAID/E&amp;E AA..</narrative>
  </description>
